 4465 \\).\n\nThus, \\( S = 2C - 4465 \\), where \\( C \\) is the number of pairs with product +1. To minimize the positive value of \\( S \\), we need to minimize \\( C \\), because \\( S \\) is directly proportional to \\( C \\).\n\nNow, \\( C \\) is the number of pairs with both numbers the same. So, \\( C = \\binom{x}{2} + \\binom{y}{2} = \\frac{x(x-1)}{2} + \\frac{y(y-1)}{2} \\).\n\nSince \\( x + y = 95 \\), we can express \\( C \\) in terms of \\( x \\) as \\( C = \\frac{x(x-1) + (95 - x)(94 - x)}{2} \\).\n\nSimplify \\( C \\):\n\\( C = \\frac{x^2 - x + (95 - x)(94 - x)}{2} \\)\n\\( = \\frac{x^2 - x + 95 \\times 94 - 95x - 94x + x^2}{2} \\)\n\\( = \\frac{2x^2 - 190x + 95 \\times 94}{4} \\)\nBut let\'s compute it step by step:\n\nFirst expand \\( (95 - x)(94 - x) \\):\n\n\\( (95 - x)(94 - x) = 95 \\times 94 - 95x - 94x + x^2 \\)\n\\( = 95 \\times 94 - 190x + x^2 \\)\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\( C = \\frac{x^2 - x + 95 \\times 94 - 190x + x^2}{2} \\)\n\\( = \\frac{2x^2 - 191x + 95 \\times 94}{2} \\)\nHence,\n\n\\( C = x^2 - \\frac{191}{2}x + \\frac{95 \\times 94}{2} \\)\n\\( = x^2 - 95.5x + \\frac{95 \\times 94}{2} \\)\n\nBut since 95 is an odd number, let\'s express \\( C \\) in terms of \\( x \\):\n\nAlternatively, since \\( x + y = 95 \\), \\( y = 95 - x \\). Then,\n\n\\( C = \\binom{x}{2} + \\binom{95 - x}{2} \\)\n\\( = \\frac{x(x - 1)}{2} + \\frac{(95 - x)(94 - x)}{2} \\)\n\\( = \\frac{x^2 - x + 95 \\times 94 - 95x - 94x + x^2}{2} \\)\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\( x^2 - x + x^2 = 2x^2 - x \\)\n\\( -95x - 94x = -190x \\)\nTherefore,\n\n\\( C = \\frac{2x^2 - x + 95 \\times 94}{2} \\)\nThus,\n\n\\( C = x^2 - \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{95 \\times 94}{2} \\)\n\nCalculate \\( \\frac{95 \\times 94}{2} \\):\n\n\\( \\frac{95 \\times 94}{2} = \\frac{(95 \\times 94)}{2} = 95 \\times 47 = 4465 \\)\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\( C = x^2 - 0.5x + 4465 \\)\nThus,\n\n\\( S = 2C - 4465 = 2(x^2 - 0.5x + 4465) - 4465 = 2x^2 - x + 4465 - 4465 = 2x^2 - x \\)\n\nSo, \\( S = 2x^2 - x \\).\n\nTo find the